Findings
- B1 [Blocker] Red case 8 asserts substring text, not the reason field.
  roles.test.ts:169 uses toContain("preset") on joined log lines. Strategy S2.4
  case 8 and S2.11 row A1 require the field assertion, and the falsification
  condition names includes('preset') as failing review. The code is correct
  (roles.ts:48-49), so the fix is test-only: parse the logged JSON and assert
  reason === 'preset'. Route to Green.
- N1 [Major] The S1 Review B OPENROUTER_DEBUG finding is still open. S2 did not
  fix it. openrouter-client.ts:18-27 passes no debugLogger, so a Worker variable
  OPENROUTER_DEBUG=1 makes the SDK log the authorization header and the request
  and response bodies (node_modules/@openrouter/sdk/esm/lib/sdks.js:59-62). No
  repository file sets the flag, so the risk stays latent. Fix in S3: pass a no-op
  debugLogger and add a test with OPENROUTER_DEBUG=1.
- N2 [Nit] The S2 Verify grep will match roles.test.ts:51, :172, and :174. These
  lines are the case-9 fixture that proves the old variable is not used. My grep
  confirms no production code matches OPENROUTER_MODEL or openrouter/free.
  Default: the verifier records the three test-file matches as the live
  complement and does not block on them.
- N3 [Nit] No test resolves two roles and asserts the second role keeps its own
  model (strategy S2.7 guardrail). The implementation is a Map keyed by role
  (providers.ts:385-387), correct by inspection. Default: add the two-role cache
  isolation test in S3.
- N4 [Nit] No package test imports the four new exports from src/index.ts
  (strategy S2.10 complement row). The role tests import from ../roles directly.
  Default: import the new exports from the package surface in an S3 test.

